<SiteLayout title="Dragon Community — Town Square" description="The public square of Dragon: people, shows, spaces, proposals and the activity that makes the network feel inhabited."><PublicPage active="community" eyebrow="TOWN SQUARE" title="A place becomes real when people care what happens here." intro="Dragon Community is being built around recognizable people, recurring programs, useful spaces and transparent participation — not an endless anonymous feed.">
<section class="town-grid">
  <article class="town-lead"><small>THE SQUARE</small><h2>What's happening in Dragon?</h2><p>Shows, openings, discussions, collaborations, releases, community decisions and milestones converge here. Visitors can watch. Members can participate. Operators can establish something people return to.</p><div class="town-actions"><a class="dr-button dr-button--primary" href="/media/">SEE WHAT'S ON</a><a class="dr-button" href="/creators/">MEET CREATORS</a></div></article>
  <aside class="town-board"><span>COMING UP</span><b>Saturday programming</b><b>Community Town Hall</b><b>New creator spaces</b><b>Open collaboration calls</b></aside>
</section>
<section class="community-pillars"><article><small>BELONG</small><h3>Member Identity</h3><p>Follow, save, discuss, build history and become recognizable without needing to turn yourself into a business.</p></article><article><small>CONTRIBUTE</small><h3>Standing + Badges</h3><p>Standing is earned through contribution. Badges preserve accomplishments and moments in Dragon history. Money does not buy reputation.</p></article><article><small>OPERATE</small><h3>Your Space</h3><p>A show, studio, shop, service, publication or community can become a persistent place with its own programming and audience.</p></article><article><small>HAVE A SAY</small><h3>Town Hall</h3><p>Some decisions are owner or staff decisions; others can be consultations, member votes or operator votes. The decision class stays explicit.</p></article></section>
<section class="town-meeting"><small>DRAGON GOVERNANCE</small><h2>Town Hall is not pretend democracy.</h2><p>Dragon remains an operated business, while community proposals and appropriate votes give members meaningful participation. Ownership, moderation, safety, editorial judgment and legal obligations remain clearly assigned.</p><div><span>OWNER DECISION</span><span>STAFF DECISION</span><span>COMMUNITY CONSULTATION</span><span>MEMBER VOTE</span><span>OPERATOR VOTE</span></div></section>
</PublicPage></SiteLayout>
